  <iati-identifier>XM-DAC-7-PPR-4000006025</iati-identifier>
  <reporting-org ref="XM-DAC-7" type="10">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ministry of Foreign Affairs of the Netherlands</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening the Power of Youth Voices for equal access to civic and political rights, service and opportunities for sustainable development.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Opportunities for youth involvement in decisions on laws, policies and programmes that impact their lives are limited. This project seeks to promote an enabling civic space and therefore strengthen the capacity, ability and participation of young people in civic engagement and in holding governments and the private sector accountable for the realization of SGDs. Specifically by 1) Promoting youth inclusion by creating inclusive platforms and shared safe spaces 2) Investing in youth-led initiatives to promote accountability 3) Strengthening youth civic participation online  and promoting youth-led civic space. The intervention will seek to ensure that lobby and advocacy efforts by political and civic actors on youth and inclusion find their way to decision-making spaces against a backdrop of the need for integrating youth in decision-making. Siasa Place and The Centre for Multiparty Democracy (CMD-Kenya) will foresee a close collaboration and joint implementation of the acivity.</narrative>
  </description>
